cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FITA — Flexible Image Transfer Alpha"
message: "If you use this software or the FITA convention, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  FITA is a FITS convention for multi-layer astronomical images that lets a
  user balance data so as to re-naturalise sliced and measured phenomena lying
  beyond the reach of human senses, while maintaining the scientific integrity
  of the measurements. Calibrated flux is held in FLUX_* extensions and
  display transparency in paired ALPHA_* extensions, so re-selecting a display
  range changes only what the eye sees and never the measured flux, verified
  bit-for-bit. It adds per-layer blend modes, non-destructive adjustment
  layers, stereo depth encoding physical ISM penetration, and IVOA ObsCore
  v1.1 provenance, while remaining a valid FITS multi-extension file readable
  by any FITS reader. Designed for multi-wavelength astronomy and the
  integration of multispectral measurements into physical models and
  astrophysical inference, FITA is intended to be multi-wavelength and
  multidisciplinary, and is at the heart of the MWVO (Multi-Wave Virtual
  Observatory).
authors:
  - given-names: "Ignacio A."
    family-names: "Cisneros"
    email: "astroobserver88@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0282-6098"
# This is the PACKAGE version (the software), not FITAVER (the format).
# They are different numbers and are allowed to differ -- see
# FITA_FORMAT_STANDARD.md section 13.1. The format described is FITAVER = 1.5;
# the package implementing it is 1.5.4. Conflating the two is what produced six
# mutually inconsistent version identities for this format, measured 2026-10-28.
# tests/test_version_concordance.py now asserts this file agrees with
# pyproject.toml and .zenodo.json, so the drift cannot recur silently.
# `date-released` is the v1.5.4 release date. Its DOI was added AFTER the tag
# was cut, because a version DOI cannot exist before its Release is published --
# so the tagged snapshot of this file never contains its own DOI. That lag is
# inherent and is not worth a further release to close; the next tag carries it.
#
# A TAG IS STILL NOT A DEPOSIT, and that distinction is worth keeping here:
# Zenodo archives Releases, not tags, and does not backfill. v1.3.0 and v1.2.1
# each needed a Release to get a DOI, and the duplicate v1.2.0 record below is
# what deleting and recreating a Release leaves behind.
version: "1.5.4"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21763301"          # concept DOI: always the newest version
# Every version DOI that exists, ENUMERATED from the Zenodo REST API on
# 2026-11-15 (GET /api/records?q=conceptdoi:... &all_versions=true), not inferred
# from this repository. Two earlier revisions of this list were wrong because
# they were reasoned out instead of looked up: the first claimed v1.2.0 was the
# only deposit, the second claimed v1.2.1 had no DOI. Both were false. If this
# list needs changing again, ask the archive.
#
# v1.2.0 appears TWICE, five minutes apart. That is the ObsCore erratum episode:
# Zenodo archives Releases and does not backfill, so the release was deleted and
# recreated to get it deposited, which left two records for one version. Cite
# 21763344, the later one, which is the record the published badge pointed to.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24239744"
    description: "Version DOI for v1.5.4 -- the newest deposit, and what the concept DOI above currently resolves to"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24239352"
    description: "Version DOI for v1.5.3 -- archived with a test file that does not import on Python 3.9; superseded by v1.5.4"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21765462"
    description: "Version DOI for v1.3.0"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21765372"
    description: "Version DOI for v1.2.1 -- the ObsCore label erratum"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21763344"
    description: "Version DOI for v1.2.0 -- permanently carries the withdrawn 'ObsCore v1.2' claim; see ERRATUM__ObsCore_version__2026-08-02.md"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21763302"
    description: "Superseded duplicate deposit of v1.2.0, 5 minutes older than 21763344; do not cite"
